<title>FRANCE: Jospin office says no decision yet on Fr Telecom.</title>
<headline>Jospin office says no decision yet on Fr Telecom.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Prime Minister Lionel Jospin has taken no decision yet on whether to proceed with the sale of a minority stake in telecoms operator France Telecom, the prime minister's office said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;There has been no decision on France Telecom,&quot; a spokesman for Jospin's office said.</p>
<p>Finance Minister Dominique Strauss-Kahn has told Socialist members of parliament he is open to a partial sale on condition the staff of the telecoms operator is consulted, according to government sources.</p>
<p>The comment from the prime minister's office was the first official confirmation that the France Telecom sale decision had yet to be taken.</p>
</text>
